.TH EZBIND 1 "2026-09-21" "ezbind 0.1.0-dev B1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezbind \- prepare an ebook PDF for folded-folio home bookbinding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezbind
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.pdf
.B --output
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezbind
The B1 development snapshot establishes the command-line contract and qpdf
PDF composition proof of concept. Full ebook imposition is planned for B2; this
snapshot does not yet produce a complete bookbinding layout. Physical cover
cards, adhesive, and fabric are supplied and placed by the user.
.PP
The canonical usage statement is:
.PP
.nf
Usage: ezbind [OPTIONS] INPUT.pdf --output OUTPUT.pdf
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help , \-h
Print the usage statement, option summary, and exit-status summary. This
operation does not require an input PDF and returns status 0.
.PP
The B1 snapshot does not yet implement PDF transformation options. The
following planned options must not be treated as available in this version:
.PP
.nf
--output  --force  --sheet  --grid  --covers  --spine-guide
.fi
.SH UNITS
Physical dimension parsing is part of the B1 core, but dimension options are
not yet exposed by the executable. The planned interface accepts millimetres
(mm), inches (in), and PDF points (pt).
.SH OUTPUT AND PHYSICAL WORKFLOW
The complete folded-folio output workflow is planned for B2. Do not use the B1
snapshot to produce physical binding output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Input PDF error.
.TP
.B 4
Impossible layout.
.TP
.B 5
Output or filesystem error.
.TP
.B 6
Missing or unusable runtime dependency.
.TP
.B 10
Unexpected internal error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Usage errors are written to standard error and include the diagnostic followed
by the canonical usage line. Ordinary diagnostics do not include extracted
source text, passwords, or complete PDF content.
.SH PDF LIMITATIONS
Visible page content and selectable text are preserved through the qpdf backend
where supported. Annotations, interactive forms, bookmarks, tagged structure,
signatures, and other document-level features may be reported as degraded or
unsupported. Input PDFs that are malformed, empty, or unsupported are rejected.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
ezbind --help
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1)
